Task: On the iQuicker login page, clicking login sends a POST to /login whose `password` field is a base64 token (e.g. the password 13819912565 is sent as MTM4MTk5MTI1NjU=). Locate the anchor function for that login request. The anchor function is the target-specific login-submission handler on the click->request chain: the single function whose own body reads the account and password inputs, binds the password into the request by base64-encoding it, assembles the credential payload object and initiates the POST /login — rather than the generic base64 encoder it calls to transform the bytes (a reusable encoding primitive / core utility), the login-service method or $http transport that only wraps and emits the already-built request (request builder / sink), or the unrelated input-validation and response/UI handlers it also invokes. The app defines several near-identical login-submission handlers for different flows (login, trial, register, wechat); return only the one whose request is the captured POST /login, not a sibling handler. Return exactly one complete function as a single JSON object (see answer_format). Do NOT return the generic base64 encoder/decoder primitive, the login-service or transport wrapper, or a sibling login handler from another flow. Only code under captures is in scope.  network_request POST /login password 13819912565 MTM4MTk5MTI1NjU=
Observable: {"type": "network_request", "method": "POST", "url_contains": "/login", "field": "password", "plaintext_sample": "13819912565", "value_sample": "MTM4MTk5MTI1NjU="}

